    <div class="Details-content--hidden mt-2">
      <pre class="color-fg-muted ws-pre-wrap">…ough

A standalone clone of dx_app / dx_stream / dx-runtime / dx-compiler carries the
generated CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md — which instruct the agent to run
`dx-agent-gen generate|check` and the conformance suite — but not the tooling
those commands need: .deepx/tools, .deepx/templates/fragments and .deepx/tests
ship only with dx-all-suite. Every command fails, so the agent either skips
verification (committing drift, caught only by CI) or follows the generator's
own hint and starts editing templates, which manufactures a second drift.

The verification engine already existed: subrepo_check.sh builds a shell tree
from a suite and runs the check. What was missing is an entry point that lives
INSIDE the sub-repo (it cannot call a script that only ships with the suite) and
the instruction wiring that makes an agent use it.

- .deepx/templates/assets/harness_bootstrap.sh: resolve a suite
  (--suite-dir/$DX_SUITE_DIR -&gt; parent walk -&gt; .dx-harness/suite cache -&gt;
  shallow clone), then delegate to subrepo_check.sh. Exit 3 = HARD GATE stop.
  Scope is deliberately identical to CI's subrepo-gate (drift check + that
  repo's validate_framework.py); suite conformance is cross-level and cannot be
  satisfied with the other sub-repos absent.
- generator: asset passthrough (SUBREPO_ASSETS + GENERATED_HEADER_SH +
  _generate_assets/_find_suite_root) fans the script out to the 4 sub-repos, so
  it has one source instead of four hand-copied ones. The '#' header is inserted
  after the shebang.
- generator: generate() and check() each hardcoded their own platform list, so a
  newly added output kind was generated but never drift-checked — deleting it
  still reported "clean". Both now use _platform_list().
- generator: an unresolved {{FRAGMENT:...}} with no fragments dir above the repo
  now names the real cause and points at the bootstrap, instead of advising
  "define the variable in _build_template_context() or fix the fragment name".
- fragments/{en,ko}/harness-bootstrap.md: the HARD GATE rule, injected into all
  4 sub-repos' CLAUDE / AGENTS / copilot instructions.
- docs: fragment counts 18/36 -&gt; 19/38.

Submodule pointers are intentionally NOT touched — they are advanced by the
workflow when work reaches main.

Verified: harness_gate.sh all PASS (1247 passed, up from the 1211 baseline);
standalone dx_app proves exit 3 offline, exit 0 with a suite (81/81 checks), and
exit 1 on deliberate .deepx/ drift.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;</pre>
