    <div class="Details-content--hidden mt-2">
      <pre class="color-fg-muted ws-pre-wrap">…failure

setup_remotes.sh iterates sync.conf's [repo NAME] sections, and dx-modelzoo had
none. A configured-but-missing checkout prints "... is not a git checkout —
skipped", but an unconfigured repo prints nothing at all, so dx-modelzoo looked
like the one repo that failed when it was simply never covered.

- sync.conf: add [repo dx-modelzoo] (before [repo dx-all-suite], per the file's
  own "nested repos before the parent that gitlinks them" rule) and add
  dx-modelzoo:dx-modelzoo to the suite's gitlinks.
- tests: assert every .gitmodules submodule has a sync.conf section, so adding a
  submodule without deciding its sync status fails loudly instead of vanishing
  from the tool's output.
- tests: test_committed_conf_refuses_to_run_unedited_with_a_hint now passes an
  empty --override. sync.override.conf is gitignored and auto-loaded, so any
  developer who had correctly created one turned this test red.

Verified: 82 ghes-sync tests pass; setup_remotes.sh --dry-run now reports
dx-modelzoo with both ghes and mirror URLs.

Note: with gitlink_check=strict, dx-modelzoo is now expected to carry the
configured branch. Offline refs suggest GHES has feature/dx-agent-dev while the
mirror side shows only main, and this machine can reach neither host — confirm
with a networked `ghes-sync.sh --dry-run` before a real sync.

