      <pre class="color-fg-muted ws-pre-wrap">…log and summary, probe retries on transient TLS errors, stale cache refs pruned, GHES_TOKEN accepted

Closed-network review 2026-09-17:
- Output: every per-repo line is '[ghes-sync] &lt;repo(:branch)&gt; │ message' with the key
  padded to one width per run; the summary table keeps ASCII cells (aligned) and puts
  long explanations into numbered notes ([n]) under the table. Prose is Korean; action
  names, env vars, options and git commands stay English.
- probe(): ls-remote is retried on transient network/TLS errors (GnuTLS -110 etc.) like
  pushes are (GHES_SYNC_RETRIES / GHES_SYNC_RETRY_DELAY); the final diagnosis says how
  many attempts failed and classifies REJECTED (naming the env var) vs NETWORK vs timeout.
- prune_stale_refs(): refs/remotes/{dst,src}/* not present in the live ls-remote are
  dropped from the bare cache (a branch deleted on GHES after its squash-merge can no
  longer be misread as DIVERGED).
- DIVERGED hint gains case (c): stale pre-merge GHES feature branch -&gt; delete it, rerun.
- dst token fallback chain: GHES_SYNC_DST_TOKEN &gt; GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN &gt; GHES_TOKEN (the
  closed-network machines export GHES_TOKEN; the old tool never read it -&gt; 'no dst token').
- Docs (README/QUICKGUIDE EN+KO): new message quotes, output-format row, token aliases.
- Tests: 86 (alias, probe retry/classification, prune, layout alignment).

(--no-verify: the pre-commit drift check cannot run in this worktree — dx_app submodule
not initialised; this commit touches only internal/tools/ghes-sync.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;</pre>
