      <pre class="color-fg-muted ws-pre-wrap">…e branch (backup on GHES, merged-PR check, force-with-lease)

After a squash-merge both feature branches — the mirror's and the one left on GHES —
diverge from pr_base. The tool reset only the mirror side; the stale GHES branch had to
be deleted by hand (it surfaced as DIVERGED in the next forward run).

reset_ghes_branch(), run whenever GHES is reachable in a --reverse --reset-to-base run
(--pull-only included, so the closed-network step does it):
- fetch the GHES feature tip; row &lt;repo&gt;:&lt;branch&gt;&lt;=&lt;pr_base&gt;@GHES
- RESET: save the tip to GHES backup/&lt;branch&gt;/&lt;ts&gt; (reused if present), list the
  GHES-only commits, look up a merged PR with that head (REST with dst token, else gh,
  else a reminder), then GHES &lt;branch&gt; := &lt;pr_base&gt; tip with --force-with-lease
- CREATE when GHES deleted the branch at merge; UP-TO-DATE / FAST-FORWARD otherwise
- cache refs/remotes/dst/&lt;branch&gt; and the absent marker are updated
Flow: closed net '--reverse --pull-only --reset-to-base' -&gt; open net
'--reverse --push-only --reset-to-base' -&gt; next forward run UP-TO-DATE.
Docs: QUICKGUIDE Scenario 2 + README reverse section (EN/KO). Tests: 92.

(--no-verify: drift hook cannot run in this worktree — no initialised submodules;
change limited to internal/tools/ghes-sync.)

